  "summary": "Six preprints show that conclusions from omics data shift with evaluation depth, scoring method, cell composition or compartment, cautioning against uniform readouts.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is that quantitative omics readouts are bounded by the compartment or analytical depth at which they are evaluated. Proteomic co-abundance benchmarks show method rankings changing with evaluation depth, and colorectal stress granule contrasts between fibroblasts and epithelium depend on scoring method and depth. Post-stroke efferocytosis signals are limited by cell composition and time rather than reflecting flux. Cochlear ageing appears compartment-specific, with weak systemic concordance and a distinct macrophage programme. Cortical GABAergic neurons show channel expression aligned with dendritic conductance load in a reinforcing direction. A sequence model conditioned on cell state predicts responses to an unseen stimulus but not stimulus-dependent genetic effects. The emphasis is on explicit reporting of depth, scoring and compartment context.",
